      "body": "### Proposal Details\n\nI read that go uses curly braces for statements, because of invissible errors when embedding code into other languages.\nI find that may have been a common issue google devs faced working with C, but I find it really niche everywhere else, like, most programmers wont ever do that kind of stuff, and yet have to use braces, introducing a considerable amount of visual noise, impacting readability and the overall aesthetic of the language.\nI suggest not replacing braces, but also adding the possibility to use indentation like python instead, same as Verse programming language does (it supports both braces and python indentation)\n\nI believe that introducing an optional indentation-based syntax will significantly enhance the developer experience in Go by reducing visual noise and improving readability for many without breaking compatibility.",
